SEO & Keyword Analytics: Nigerian Consumer Banking (Stage 4)

Project Overview
This project provides a data-driven analysis of the digital footprint and SEO (Search Engine Optimization) strategies of the top 15 Nigerian banks. 
By analyzing search volumes, keyword difficulty, and paid competition, I evaluated how financial institutions leverage online visibility to drive customer acquisition for core services like loans and account opening.

Objectives
Identify the dominant players in the Nigerian banking digital landscape.
Categorize thousands of keywords into functional business groups (e.g., Loans & Credit,Digital Banking).
Analyze the correlation between SEO "Keyword Difficulty" and business value (CPC/PPC).
Visualize growth trends to identify mid-tier banks gaining significant search momentum.

Technical Workflow
Data Acquisition:
Extracted keyword data using Google Ads Keyword Planner and Mangools Keyword Finder.
Gathered metrics including Average Monthly Search Volume, Cost Per Click (CPC), and Keyword Difficulty (KD).

Data Cleaning & Categorization (Excel):
Standardized bank names and removed duplicate keyword entries.
Used string matching to group keywords into 8 strategic categories: Loans & Credit, Online Banking, Account Opening, Bank Codes, Branch/ATM Locations, etc.

Data Visualization (Power BI):
Imported the cleaned dataset into Power BI for advanced modeling.

Built an interactive dashboard featuring:

Market Share Analysis: Ranking banks by total search volume (Zenith Bank leading).

Difficulty vs. Payoff: A matrix comparing keyword difficulty against Paid Competition (PPC).

Growth Analytics: Identifying banks with the highest "Interest Growth Rate" (e.g., Wema, Keystone).

Key Insights
Market Dominance: Zenith Bank, First Bank, and Access Bank control the majority of the search market share.

High-Value Competition: The most expensive keywords (highest PPC) are "Account Opening" and "Loans," proving these are the primary drivers for digital revenue.

The "Digital Shift": Keywords related to "Internet Banking" and "Mobile Apps" have the highest difficulty scores, reflecting the intense competition in the Fintech space.

Emerging Players: Mid-tier banks like Wema Bank are showing rapid growth in search interest, likely due to successful digital-first branding (e.g., ALAT).

Tools Used
SEO Tools: Google Keyword Planner, Mangools.
Data Cleaning: Microsoft Excel (Pivot Tables & Data Formatting).
Data Visualization: Power BI (DAX, Interactive Reporting).
